fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: the_unfinished
name: The Unfinished
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  # v0.3: Boss, durability 8, attack +2, two specials (the Great Work, Conscription), rating 14.
  level: 4
  role: boss
  armor: 0
  morale: 12
  weapon: Whatever tool the work needs next
  wants: The great work completed.
  special: 'CONSCRIPTION — once per scene, it sets a character a task. They may spend their
    action doing it, or refuse. Refusing is free, but every Waiting One in the scene treats
    them as an obstruction from then on. A character who completes a task is staff: it will
    not attack them.'
  when_bloodied: It stops assigning and does the work itself, at speed, with its own hands.
    Its attacks target the site, not the party, and every exchange the work visibly advances.
    The party has to decide whether that is a problem.
  tells: Something at the centre of the work looks at you, then past you, and makes a gesture
    that plainly means take the other end.
  breaks: 'Never breaks; the work is not finishable, and it will not stop for anything short
    of the party making it so. Bring it a credible plan and it will listen at length, mid-fight,
    and a good plan ends the fight: it lays down the tools, and so does everyone else.'
  twists:
  - The quarry that fed the work closed a century ago, and somebody still owns it.
  - The district behind the wall is populated, and nobody there wants anything resolved.
  - One of the Waiting Ones was reassigned from a job three streets away and would like to
    go back to it.
  - The work is a road through the mountains, and the party needs the road.
  - The authority that could approve a change of plan has a successor office, and it is sitting
    today.
  - The thing the wall was built to keep out stopped existing long ago.
  nastier: It can conscript once every exchange instead of once per scene.
  description: >-
    A foreman, or a prior, or a harbourmaster — whatever the place needed most. It is at the
    centre of the work, and the work has grown. Around it the others labour at jobs that were
    never theirs, on a project none of them began, and it is going to be finished.
  notes: >-
    Level 4 Boss: no overrides. The Great Work is what it is rather than a rule, so it lives
    in WANTS; Conscription is the card's gimmick. Fearless (morale 12).


    Administrative: it does not fight so much as assign. It spends its first exchange assessing
    and its second conscripting, and it has never once left the work. Its first target is
    whoever is disrupting the most labour. Rated as a Boss; intended to be finished rather
    than beaten.


    Appears: one, with four to twelve Waiting Ones, at a site where something large was left
    half-done.
  reskin_of: null
